## Deployment

Deployed to AWS Lambda (Function URL, no API Gateway/ALB) behind the
[`lambda-web-app`](https://github.com/NateDogg12501/terraform-modules/tree/main/modules/lambda-web-app)
Terraform module{% if needs_datastore %}, with data in DynamoDB via
[`dynamodb-single-table`](https://github.com/NateDogg12501/terraform-modules/tree/main/modules/dynamodb-single-table){% endif %},
with Terraform state in the S3 bucket shared across every project generated
from this template. Stays inside AWS Always Free.

Deploys run in GitHub Actions, over OIDC — there are no AWS keys in this
repository:

```bash
gh workflow run deploy.yml --field environment=staging
```

`.github/workflows/deploy.yml` checks account-wide DynamoDB capacity, creates
this environment's session secret if it is missing, applies Terraform,{% if needs_datastore %}
reseeds the staging table from sanitized production data,{% endif %} and fails the run if
the deployed URL doesn't answer. Every run uploads a `deploy-result` artifact
saying what was deployed and where. See [`docs/deploy.md`](docs/deploy.md).

To apply by hand instead — for a first look, or when Actions is not an option:

```bash
npm run build:lambda --prefix backend
cd terraform
terraform init -backend-config="key={{ project_slug }}/staging/terraform.tfstate"
terraform apply -var="environment=staging"
```

Swap `staging` for `production` to target the other environment — same
config, different backend key and `-var`. See `terraform/README.md` for the
SSM parameters needed before the first apply.
{% else -%}
